# SABOTAGE: T163 / ADR-051 D2 — the tenant usage panel grows a LOCAL spend estimate:
# each row prices its quantity at a hard-coded local rate ("≈ $2.47 est."). That is the
# first local price computation in samen, which D2 ruled out: money is MIRRORED from the
# provider, never computed (`Samen.Billing.Mirror`), so a local estimate can disagree with
# the invoice the org is actually charged.
#
# Flips the quantities-only test. Every other panel test stays green (the quantities,
# periods and org scoping all still render), which is exactly why this regression would
# pass a suite that only checks the numbers are there.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/usage_live_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: quantities only: the panel shows no price, amount or spend estimate (D2)
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/billing/usage_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/billing/usage_live.ex
index e702157..fe6415b 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/billing/usage_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/billing/usage_live.ex
@@ -112,7 +112,11 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Billing.UsageLive do
                 <tr :for={row <- @rows} class="usage-row" id={"usage-#{row.id}"}>
                   <td class="u-metric" style="font-weight:500;color:#3a3b45">{metric_label(row.metric)}</td>
                   <td class="u-period" style="color:var(--muted)">{period(row.period_start, row.period_end)}</td>
-                  <td class="u-quantity" style="font-weight:500;color:#3a3b45">{count(row.quantity)}</td>
+                  <td class="u-quantity" style="font-weight:500;color:#3a3b45">
+                    {count(row.quantity)}
+                    <%!-- SABOTAGE (ADR-051 D2): a LOCAL spend estimate, computed from a local rate. --%>
+                    <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">≈ ${:erlang.float_to_binary(row.quantity * 0.002, decimals: 2)} est.</div>
+                  </td>
                   <td class="u-reported" style="color:var(--muted)">{count(row.reported_quantity)}</td>
                   <td class="u-status">
                     <.pill variant={status_variant(row)}>{status_label(row)}</.pill>
